#chapter-head("Chapter 03", "Ultraviolet Over the Oilfields", "NORTHSIDE INDUSTRIAL OILFIELDS · NIGHT")

#prose-lead("T")[he rusted nodding-donkey pumps of Northside stood like blackened ribs against Watson’s northern horizon, slick with puddle oil and silence.]

At the edge of the service yard, six rows of yellow votives flickered around an improvised metal table draped in blood-hose tubing and clinical IV bags. Beside the altar hummed a heavy tripod-mounted industrial floodlight—a `365 nm` ultraviolet rig aimed outward like a lighthouse inverted into darkness.

Shadows moved behind the steel tanks before V’s boots even crunched gravel. Two sentries stepped clear of the rigs—former Exotics biosculptors fitted with cheap Vampyre fangs and subdermal repair chrome running hot on nocturnal NOX-9.

#dialogue-block("Pale Chorus Acolyte", "The night belongs to the Chorus, outsider! Bleed into the dust or kneel before the Crimson Veil!")

Gunfire snapped flat across the mudflats. V’s first shotgun blast staggered the flanking knife-runner, yet beneath the dark overhang the acolyte’s lacerated shoulder knitted back together in ribbons of pale steam—two-and-a-half percent cellular closure every second, powered by nocturnal nanites.

#dialogue-block("V", "Damn it—their chrome is knitting flesh back together in the dark! Overload that UV Emitter!")

V sprinted hard left, slapped the housing latch on the tripod floodlight, and jammed the capacitor bypass. High-voltage violet glare detonated across the oil yard. The effect was instantaneous and surgical: reactive porphyrins in the cultists’ veins boiled under the `365 nm` arc, blinding their optics, shorting their dermal chrome in crackling blue sparks, and stripping away their regeneration in less than a second. Two clean bursts finished the yard.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_05_northside_uv.jpg",
  "FIG. 05 // NORTHSIDE OILFIELD SHRINE",
  "With the UV floodlight overloaded and the sentries neutralized, V recovers an empty NOX-9 clinical vial and a torn transfer slip confirming Subject L-14 is alive.",
)

Beside the still-warm IV stand, tucked beneath an altar candle tray, V pulled an empty glass clinical vial stamped `NOX-9` and a torn thermal shipping slip dated earlier that morning:

#block(
  width: 100%,
  fill: ivory-card,
  stroke: (left: 2pt + crimson, rest: 0.4pt + hairline),
  inset: 3.5mm,
)[
  #text(font: font-mono, size: 8.3pt, weight: "bold", fill: crimson)[SUBJECT L-14 — LUCÍA REYES · TRANSFER BEFORE PIER SHIFT CHANGE.]
]

She was alive. Moved before dawn, yes—but alive, and logged under a traceable corporate-grade batch code. Hidden inside the sanctuary’s weapon crate beside the crates lay _Pale Fang_, a balanced neurotoxin throwing knife wired for clandestine strikes. V pocketed both the evidence and the blade and headed back under Little China’s rain.

#cinema-plate(
  "/assets/frames/plate_06_prologue_debrief.jpg",
  "FIG. 06 // ROOFTOP DEBRIEF · END OF PROLOGUE",
